71|// visitor's browser send a `mode:"no-cors"` `text/plain` POST (a CORS
72|// simple request, no preflight), spending owner budget and draining the
73|// shared daily spend cap from many IPs. Our own clients always send
74|// `Content-Type: application/json` from the same origin, so anything
75|// else is not ours. Pure: reads headers and the request URL only, and
76|// never logs header values.
